Package: vim-copilot
Version: @VERSION@
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: ca-certificates, git
Suggests: vim
Provides: editor
Homepage: https://www.vim.org
Description: Vi IMproved with native GitHub Copilot support
 A fork of Vim @UPSTREAM_VERSION@ that implements GitHub Copilot directly in the
 C core, with no plugin manager, no VimScript shim and no Node.js runtime.
 .
 The editor talks to a bundled copilot-language-server over Vim's built-in
 LSP channel mode and adds a single :copilot command providing:
 .
  * chat in a dedicated window, with streamed replies
  * slash commands over a range: explain, fix, tests, doc, simplify
  * inline "ghost text" completions, optionally triggered automatically
  * an agent mode that can run shell commands and read files, each of which
    always requires explicit interactive confirmation
 .
 This package installs as vim-copilot and keeps all of its runtime files
 under /usr/share/vim-copilot. It shares no file with the vim, vim-common,
 vim-runtime or xxd packages, registers nothing with update-alternatives,
 and can therefore be installed alongside the distribution's own Vim.
